 **Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
 
+### Specialty directory
+
+<a id="req-vet-003"></a>
+
+Staff ask the veterinarian directory's question in reverse: which veterinarians hold a given specialty. The clinic answers it with a specialty directory, which lists every specialty the clinic knows by its stored name `[REQ-VET-003]`. Each specialty is shown with the veterinarians holding it, each named first name then last name. Every specialty appears on a single page, and a veterinarian holding no specialty appears under none of them — the page lists specialties, not the whole roster. The page is reachable by requesting its address alone: nothing in the system links to it `[REQ-VET-003]`. Its own wording follows `[REQ-LANG-002]` as on every page, while a stored specialty name is data and appears as stored.
+
+**Done when:**
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given the clinic's specialties, when the specialty directory is opened, then every stored specialty is listed by its stored name.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty that veterinarians hold, when the directory is opened, then each holder is named first name then last name, such as "Helen Leary".
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the directory is opened, then that veterinarian appears nowhere on the page.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given every specialty the clinic knows, when the directory is opened, then all of them appear on one page, with no paging.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given any page of the system, when it is rendered, then it carries no navigation entry or link to the specialty directory.
+
+**Edge cases:**
+1. A specialty no veterinarian holds is still listed, shown as held by none rather than left blank.
+2. A veterinarian holding two specialties is shown under each of them.
+3. The specialties, and the veterinarians within each, are presented in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one.
+
+**Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
+
